course: dictionary
lesson: 7251
title: Pied: one word, two languages
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Pied» is an adjective in English. It means having patches of two or more colours, especially black and white, like a magpie or a pied wagtail. Look for the patches: that is the clue.
explain: Pied is also part of a famous story. «The Pied Piper of Hamelin» is a piper in colourful clothes from an old German legend, who leads away the rats and then the children. Because it is a name, it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Pied is also a French word. «Pied» means foot, and «à pied» means on foot. In the song «Tête, épaules, genoux et pieds», pieds is the plural: more than one foot. Context tells you which language you are in, so ask yourself: is this an English sentence or a French one?
fact: Pied means having patches of two or more colours.
fact: Pied wagtails and magpies are birds with black and white markings.
fact: The Pied Piper is a character in an old German legend from Hamelin.
fact: In French, «pied» means foot, and it is said roughly «pee-AY».
fact: «Pieds» is the plural form, as in «Tête, épaules, genoux et pieds», which means head, shoulders, knees and toes.
exercise: «Look at the pied wagtail on the wall.» What does pied mean here? | Very hungry | Very fast | *Having patches of two or more colours | Made of wood
exercise: In the story, the Pied Piper leads away the rats. Who is the Pied Piper? | A French teacher who sings | A farmer who keeps cows | A bird with black and white wings | *A piper in colourful clothes from an old German legend
exercise: In French, «pied» means which English word? | Head | *Foot | Hand | Knee
test: In the French song «Savez-vous planter les choux ?», le pied is one of the body parts. Which English word does le pied mean? | *Foot | Nose | Elbow | Knee
test: «À pied» means on foot. Which English phrase is the best meaning of «à pied»? | Under the sea | *On foot | In a car | Riding a bike
exam: «The pied magpie flew over the field.» Which meaning of pied fits this sentence? | *Having patches of two or more colours | Very fast | A piper in a legend | On foot, the French way
